# Architecture (adapted from LandLord `architecture.mdc`, audit 2026-11)

## Layers and import direction
```
features → domains → shared → core
```
- **features/<name>/** imports `@domains/*`, `@shared/*` and `@core/*`. **Never another feature** (`@features/*` or `../../<other>/`).
  Only `app.routes.ts` reaches into features, through lazy `loadComponent`/`loadChildren`.
- **domains/<entity>/** (business entities used by 2+ features: API service, models, enums, endpoints, widgets)
  imports `@shared/*`, `@core/*` and lower-ranked domains only. Ranks: `access` 0, `team` 1 (team may use access).
- **shared/** is domain-agnostic presentational UI and pure utils. It may use `@core/*` primitives, never `@domains/*` or `@features/*`.
- **core/** is app-wide singletons and infrastructure (auth/session, http, error, i18n, theme, loading, routing, layout). It never
  imports features. Only `core/layout` may use `@domains/*`.
- Cross-layer imports use the aliases `@core @domains @shared @features @env`. Within a layer, use relative imports.
- Enforced by `no-restricted-imports` blocks in `eslint.config.js`. `npm run lint` must stay at 0 problems.

## Placement decision
1. Used by one feature → `features/<name>/…`
2. Used by 2+ features and tied to a business entity → `domains/<entity>/…`
3. Used by 2+ features and domain-agnostic → `shared/…`
4. App-wide plumbing (session, http, errors, layout chrome) → `core/…`

## Feature folder contract
`<name>.routes.ts` · `pages/` (routed components, `*.page.ts`) · `components/` (feature UI, dialogs) · `services/`
(facades and stores that hold real logic; no pass-throughs) · `models/` · `enums/` · `constants/` (`<name>.endpoints.ts`) · `utils/`.
Types never live in components. There are no re-export shims: import a type from its owner.

## Migration status
The audit (docs/audit/2026-11/findings.md) is moving the remaining legacy layout into this shape: root `constants/`,
`models/` and `enums/`; `core/api`; `core/payments`; and the six-domain `features/workspace`. Don't add files to those locations.
